  "published": "2026-08-31T00:23:48.76Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Project templates: ExtractSampleData is implemented for every standard template, so the headless `template-create --data-dir` command (Designer 1.3.24) places the sample SQLite database without the GUI.\n- Selenium tests: headless `selenium-test-init` (extract a ready-to-run NUnit + Selenium test project: shared WebDriverManager with login, DataManager on Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.DbAccess for test data, LoginForm, smoke test; copies the design project's data sources and connection strings into testsettings(.local).json) and `pageobject` (generate the Selenium PageObjects of a design project; same generator as Tools > Export PageObject). The Claude Code workspace gets Docs/SeleniumTestGuide.md.\n- Claude Code workspace: can now be deployed into a folder that already has its own CLAUDE.md (e.g. the root of a host solution from Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Starter). That CLAUDE.md is preserved and the workspace rules are written to ClaudeCodeForDesigner/WorkspaceRules.md instead. Rules updated: design settings first, scripts second, C# last; headless `deploy` for FileSystem targets; host customization reference (_specs/HostCustomization.md).\n- Export PageObject: generated page objects now add the using directives for the Selenium driver namespaces of every field library in use (Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras.SeleniumDrivers, Codeer.LowCode.Bindings.Blazor-ApexCharts.SeleniumDrivers; other bindings via SeleniumPageObjectBuilder.AddDriverNamespace or the \".SeleniumDrivers\" naming convention), and no longer emit search drivers for fields that have no search control.",
